tics.dart:5:    final config = PostHogConfig('phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI');\nlib/analytics.dart:6:    config.host = 'https://eu.i.posthog.com';\nlib/analytics.dart:7:    config.captureApplicationLifecycleEvents = true;\nlib/analytics.dart:11:    await Posthog().setup(config);\nlib/analytics.dart:15:      Posthog().capture(eventName: event, properties: props);\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:3:# PostHog session replay not working in Flutter? Add PostHogWidget\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:5:PostHog can record videos of real user sessions, so you can watch where people\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:10:Here is what we had: the `posthog_flutter` SDK set up, \"Record user sessions\"\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:13:`PosthogObserver` on the router. Every checklist item we could find was ticked.\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:14:PostHog's troubleshooting page covers sampling, retention and disabled\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:17:So I guessed. I changed settings in the PostHog console. I initialized the SDK\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:22:PostHog support gave us the answer. On mobile, Flutter replay is built from\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:24:`PostHogWidget`. If it doesn't wrap your `MaterialApp`, the SDK still records\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:25:taps and other events, but it has no frames to send, so a replay never\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:38:Read-only. Preconditions: a Flutter app that depends on `posthog_flutter` and\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:39:expects session replay.\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:40:1. `grep -rn \"posthog_flutter\" pubspec.yaml` — the package must be there.\nnotes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md:41:2. `grep -rn \"sessi