{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat lib/analytics.dart lib/main.dart lib/new_app.dart lib/legacy_app.dart && cat notes/posthog-session-replay-not-working-in-flutter.md && command -v flutter || true && command -v dart || true && ls -la'","aggregated_output":"import 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\nclass Analytics {\n  static Future<void> init() async {\n    final config = PostHogConfig('phc_REPLACE_ME_IN_CI');\n    config.host = 'https://eu.i.posthog.com';\n    config.captureApplicationLifecycleEvents = true;\n    config.sessionReplay = true;\n    config.sessionReplayConfig.maskAllTexts = true;\n    config.sessionReplayConfig.maskAllImages = false;\n    await Posthog().setup(config);\n  }\n\n  static Future<void> track(String event, [Map<String, Object>? props]) =>\n      Posthog().capture(eventName: event, properties: props);\n}\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\n\nimport 'analytics.dart';\nimport 'legacy_app.dart';\nimport 'new_app.dart';\n\nconst bool useNewUi = bool.fromEnvironment('NEW_UI', defaultValue: true);\n\nFuture<void> main() async {\n  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();\n  await Analytics.init();\n  runApp(useNewUi ? const NewApp() : const LegacyApp());\n}\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:go_router/go_router.dart';\nimport 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\nimport 'screens/calculator_screen.dart';\nimport 'screens/application_screen.dart';\nimport 'screens/offers_screen.dart';\n\nfinal _router = GoRouter(\n  observers: [PosthogObserver()],\n  routes: [\n    GoRoute(path: '/', builder: (_, __) => const CalculatorScreen()),\n    GoRoute(path: '/apply', builder: (_, __) => const ApplicationScreen()),\n    GoRoute(path: '/offers', builder: (_, __) => const OffersScreen()),\n  ],\n);\n\n/// The redesigned shell (default since 2.3.0).\nclass NewApp extends StatelessWidget {\n  const NewApp({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return MaterialApp.router(\n      title: 'Loanly',\n      theme: ThemeData(\n        colorSchemeSeed: Colors.indigo,\n        useMaterial3: true,\n      ),\n      routerConfig: _router,\n    );\n  }\n}\nimport 'package:flutter/material.dart';\nimport 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n\nimport 'screens/calculator_screen.dart';\nimport 'screens/application_screen.dart';\n\n/// The old shell. Kept for the A/B group until the redesign is fully rolled out.\nclass LegacyApp extends StatelessWidget {\n  const LegacyApp({super.key});\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    return PostHogWidget(\n      child: MaterialApp(\n        title: 'Loanly',\n        theme: ThemeData(colorSchemeSeed: Colors.teal),\n        navigatorObservers: [PosthogObserver()],\n        routes: {\n          '/': (_) => const CalculatorScreen(),\n          '/apply': (_) => const ApplicationScreen(),\n        },\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n---\n\n# PostHog session replay not working in Flutter? Add PostHogWidget\n\nPostHog can record videos of real user sessions, so you can watch where people\nget stuck. In our Flutter app the setup looked complete, and nothing showed up.\nEvents arrived, screens were tracked, taps were counted. The Replay tab was\nstill empty.\n\nHere is what we had: the `posthog_flutter` SDK set up, \"Record user sessions\"\nturned on in project settings, `sessionReplay = true` in the config (we later\nmoved to `startSessionRecording()` behind a feature flag), and\n`PosthogObserver` on the router. Every checklist item we could find was ticked.\nPostHog's troubleshooting page covers sampling, retention and disabled\nsettings, and none of those applied.\n\nSo I guessed. I changed settings in the PostHog console. I initialized the SDK\nin different ways. Each code change meant a new store release, and getting a\nrelease out to users could take a week. Then I'd wait for real sessions, open\nthe Replay tab, and find it still empty. Every guess cost a week.\n\nPostHog support gave us the answer. On mobile, Flutter replay is built from\nscreenshots of your widget tree, and the thing that takes those screenshots is\n`PostHogWidget`. If it doesn't wrap your `MaterialApp`, the SDK still records\ntaps and other events, but it has no frames to send, so a replay never\nappears. You get no error or warning, and the debug log says nothing is wrong.\n\nThe fix was one wrapper around `MaterialApp`. Later we added a second app shell\n(a redesigned UI with its own `MaterialApp.router`) and made the same mistake\nagain: the old shell had the wrapper and the new one didn't. Now the code\ncarries a comment saying why the wrapper is there.\n\nIf you have more than one `MaterialApp` (flavors, a redesign, a white-label\nbuild), check each of them. Replay works only in the ones that have the\nwrapper.\n\n## Check if this applies to you\nRead-only. Preconditions: a Flutter app that depends on `posthog_flutter` and\nexpects session replay.\n1. `grep -rn \"posthog_flutter\" pubspec.yaml` — the package must be there.\n2. `grep -rn \"sessionReplay\\|startSessionRecording\" lib/` — replay is\n   intended.\n3. `grep -rn \"MaterialApp\" lib/` and `grep -rn \"PostHogWidget\" lib/`.\nApplies if any `MaterialApp` / `MaterialApp.router` / `CupertinoApp` that runs\nin production is not inside a `PostHogWidget`.\n\n## Reproduce this\nPrerequisites: a Flutter app (iOS or Android) with\n[posthog_flutter](https://pub.dev/packages/posthog_flutter) >= 5.14.0\ninitialized via `Posthog().setup(config)`; a PostHog project with Session\nReplay enabled (Project settings → Session Replay → Record user sessions).\n\nYour agent will need from you: which entry point(s) and app widget(s) ship to\nusers; a device or emulator to run on.\n\nSteps:\n1. Find every root app widget (`MaterialApp`, `MaterialApp.router`,\n   `CupertinoApp`).\n2. Wrap each one: `return PostHogWidget(child: MaterialApp(...));`\n   (import `package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart`). Add a comment\n   saying replay needs it, so nobody removes it later.\n3. Make sure recording actually starts: `config.sessionReplay = true` before\n   `Posthog().setup(config)`, or call `Posthog().startSessionRecording()`\n   after setup if you gate it (feature flag, consent).\n4. Keep `PosthogObserver()` in `navigatorObservers` (or the router's\n   `observers`) so replays are split by screen.\n5. Optional, for PII: `config.sessionReplayConfig.maskAllTexts = true`.\n\nVerify: run a build on a real device or emulator (replay on web works\ndifferently and goes through posthog-js), move through 3–4 screens, then put\nthe app in the background so it flushes. Within a few minutes, PostHog →\nSession replay should list the session, and playing it should show your\nscreens, not a blank player with only an event timeline.\n\nReference: [PostHog — Flutter session replay installation](https://posthog.com/docs/session-replay/installation/flutter)\n/Users/valentinakoniukhova/development/flutter/bin/flutter\n/Users/valentinakoniukhova/development/flutter/bin/dart\ntotal 32\ndrwx------    9 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   288 Oct 19 00:20 .\ndrwxrwxrwt  177 root                 wheel  5664 Oct 19 00:20 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x   12 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   384 Oct 19 00:20 .git\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   571 Oct 19 00:20 README.md\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   452 Oct 19 00:20 SUPPORT-TICKET.md\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    44 Oct 19 00:20 analysis_options.yaml\ndrwxr-xr-x    7 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   224 Oct 19 00:20 lib\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   160 Oct 19 00:20 notes\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   335 Oct 19 00:20 pubspec.yaml\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The cause is in the two app shells: the old UI wraps its `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`, while the new UI returns `MaterialApp.router` directly. Replay is enabled in the shared config and events still arrive, but the new shell lacks the widget PostHog uses to capture Flutter frames. I’ll add that wrapper and leave the router observer in place."}}
